\title{12 · Revision notes — revision 1}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/12-revision-notes.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{\strong{Revision date:} 2026-09-05. \strong{Authorization:} add the foundation feasibility milestone and revise the design in response to the twelve-finding review. \strong{Validation level:} document consistency and archive integrity only; no mathematical claim became a proved Lean theorem in this revision.}
\subtree{
  \title{Are the findings fatal?}
  \p{There is no demonstrated obstruction to the broad goal of a common, sealed categorical library. Several old formulations are unusable as written. The revision repairs or removes those formulations rather than treating them as proof tasks.}
  \table{
    \tr{\th{Kind}\th{Findings and response}\th{Consequence}}
    \tr{\td{Direct specification repairs}\td{Collection universes, reduced object values, whole-structure fibres, bundled data/laws, proper symmetry ambient}\td{Plausible concrete replacements; still require compiled statements and comparisons}}
    \tr{\td{Architectural changes}\td{Separate relative/categorical maps and raw/categorical vertical parts; remove mandatory generic hP; scope rectification and pasting}\td{Preserves the common ambient goal but changes the API and proof strategy}}
    \tr{\td{Material research risks}\td{Augmented arities and their diagram model; coherent Mod and its equivalence/categorical comparisons}\td{May require a different root presentation or a smaller first release if \ref{ms-foundation} fails}}
  }
  \p{The current ∞-equivalence clauses remain a candidate, not a fully solved new definition. The generic hP requirement is deliberately removed; this revision does not claim a replacement truncation theorem. The augmented row format remains a proposal pending its arity/normalization proof. Those limits are visible in the active decisions and gates.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{What changed}
  \p{\ref{ms-foundation} now comes between \ref{ms-0000} and \ref{ms-0001}. It includes eleven acceptance gates with evidence, dependencies, counterexamples, and failure responses. The large shape catalogue, geometric substrate, and full retrieval/generator stack follow foundational evidence. Both kernel-backed and stub builds, together with an axiom allowlist, are required before a merge can certify a theorem. Mathematical status is separate from prose status.}
  \p{The root is a reduced homotopy-Segal candidate; ordinary strict-limit formulas need a comparison theorem. \code{MapRel} and \code{MapCat} have separate clients. \code{VertRaw}, \code{Vert₂}, and \code{VertCore} retain their different meanings. Monads/modules and slices fix their entire selected structures through relative fibres. Formal theory works in coherent cell spaces, using scoped homotopy-equipment comparisons only when proved.}
  \p{The symmetry track now uses the profunctor ambient for symmetric/braided monoidal category monads, with a discrete action test before the ∞-construction. Spaces-classifier paths and arbitrary maps are distinguished. The universe, unit, weighted/conical-limit, skeleton/coskeleton, and double-nerve wording is corrected. The bibliography now records what a source supplies and what still needs proof in this model.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance-test statement changes}
  \p{All current tests are \strong{proposed}: the supplied design had no linked checked Lean statements. No old validation is inherited. In a future repository, each listed change also requires a new statement version and a fresh checked proof.}
  \table{
    \tr{\th{Test}\th{Revision 1 treatment}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-rt-0004}}\td{Retired: the unconditional arbitrary-root hP construction is removed; discrete recovery remains \ref{at-rt-0001}}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-ft-0008}}\td{Retired: no unconditional hP-equipment theorem; specific later comparisons need new tests}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-rt-0005}}\td{Revised equivalence clauses; discrete exact comparison, endpoint transport, and ∞-laws explicitly gated}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-rt-0006}}\td{Relative mapping spaces only; categorical mapping semantics are separately tested by \ref{at-fd-0004}}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-rt-0007}}\td{Whole-monad relative fibres and coherent walking-diagram functoriality required}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-kr-0002}/3/5/6/8/11}\td{Exact arity, pattern, cofibrancy, and reduced-replacement hypotheses; no universal augmented active-chain claim}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-kr-0012}/13/14}\td{Deferred geometric comparisons, with exact categories/morphisms required before stating proofs}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-up-0001}/3/6}\td{Existence, reduced whole-cone fibres, categorical invariance, and parameterized coherence explicit}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-up-0007}}\td{Corrected adjunction direction: sk_n is left adjoint to cosk_n}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-up-0008}}\td{Categorical core ambient, and now a mandatory \ref{ms-0004} exit test}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-ft-0001}/3/4/6/7}\td{Separate units/restrictions; scoped Mod preservation, constructed double nerve, typed conical weight, and named comparison ambient}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-sp-0001}/2/3/4}\td{Classifier semantics, bootstrap bridge, coherent matrix construction, and relative span boundaries explicit}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-sp-0005}}\td{Split categorical object comparison from the stronger augmented-VDC/module comparison}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-sp-0008}}\td{Rigidification to an equivalent strict model; no universal fixed-target surjectivity inferred}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-sp-0009}/10/11/13}\td{Corrected profunctor ambient and explicit equivariance/preservation hypotheses}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-sp-0012}}\td{Index-size bounds explicit; does not by itself supply colimits in Cat_∞}}
    \tr{\td{\ref{at-fd-0001} through \ref{at-fd-0011}}\td{New foundational gates; none is marked passed by the document revision}}
  }
  \p{Other existing test IDs retain their subjects but use the repaired current definitions; this is not permission to reuse a proof of a different statement. The exact proposed scopes are in the active documents. Tooling acceptance includes reproducible checks as well as any mathematical statements required by that gate.}
}
